From ef32fcfe43e384941656bd13121078d5de5a5157 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:18:13 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 56/62] Input: a second player's gamepad for ports with local
 multiplayer

While a port wants one (VulkanRenderer::set_second_pad_wanted, or
hle_extension::want_second_pad), a gamepad other than player 1's is opened
as player 2's and read with the same bindings and tuning into second_pad(),
never into the game's own pad. Off by default, so a second pad otherwise
stays a spare for player 1 as before. Extension interface 6 adds
want_second_pad() and second_pad().

The input script gets pad2, axis2, detach2 and attach2 steps on a second
virtual gamepad with its own vendor and product ids: with the first pad's,
SDL gave it the first pad's mapping and gamepad name. The renderer tells the
script's pads apart by their joystick names.

Checked with Dissidia 012 on Windows, with virtual pads only: player 2's pad
opened as player 2's and drove the opponent, unplugging and plugging it in
again was seen by the port, and with no port asking for it no second pad was
opened. Not tried with real controllers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
